# Rule 00. Zones and vocabulary

Language-agnostic. The words below are used by rules 01, 02, 03 and 06 and by the
runtime appendices (`runtime-svelte.mdc`, `runtime-react.mdc`, `runtime-vue.mdc`; Solid reads like React, and the
template runtimes templ, Twig, Jinja2 and Latte are generated only: their output is held by the kit-compose tests and `ui-gates source`, and the
adapters of the rules live in `packages/tooling/rules/src/rules`).

## Zones

| Zone | What lives there | Rules 01 to 06 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kit (`{kit}`) | primitives and utils: the only place that knows host tags | Do not apply. Raw HTML, dynamic tags and computed ARIA are allowed. |
| Composition | blocks, composite components, app screens and templates | Apply. |
| Generated | any file with a `Code generated by ... DO NOT EDIT.` header (`packages/kit-compose/<rt>`, `apps/host-*/gen`, `packages/shared/app`) | No hand edits (`compose:check` regenerates in memory and fails on a difference). The rules still apply: fix the spec, the authoring builder, the kit-compose map or the emitter. |

`{kit}` is a placeholder for the kit dirs of the package at hand. The UI8Kit 3 primitives themselves live in
`packages/kit/<rt>` (outside every rule zone, installed by `ui8kit`). In `packages/kit-compose/<rt>` of the TypeScript
runtimes the kit zone is `src/compose`, `src/icons`, `src/presets`, `src/utils` and `src/styles`.

## Where the paths come from

Every package or app declares its own zones in the `ui8kit` field of its `package.json`:

```json
"ui8kit": { "runtime": "vue", "generated": true, "kit": ["src/compose", "src/icons", "src/presets", "src/utils", "src/styles"], "composition": ["src/blocks", "src/components"], "blockRoot": ["src/blocks"] }
```

- `runtime`: `svelte`, `react`, `vue`, `solid`, `templ`, `twig`, `jinja2` or `latte`.
- `kit`, `composition`: dirs or files relative to the package.
- `blockRoot`: the part of the composition whose files must open on `Block` (blocks and screens).
- `generated`: `true` when compose-gen writes the package (the field is then set by the generator, `packages/kit-compose/src/hosts.ts`, not by hand).

`bun packages/tooling/bin/zones.mjs --write` assembles the catalog `rules/zones.json`.
`bun run check` (group `rules`) fails when the catalog is stale. Anything outside
both zones (plain TypeScript, data, entry files) is not scanned by the composition rules.

Current catalog (see `rules/zones.json` for the source of truth):

| Package | Runtime | Kit | Composition | Block root |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `packages/kit-compose/{svelte,react,vue,solid}` | each | `src/compose`, `src/icons`, `src/presets`, `src/utils`, `src/styles` | `src/blocks`, `src/components` | `src/blocks` and the frame components |
| `apps/host-{svelte,react,vue,solid}` | each | `gen/runtime` | `gen/App.*` (the host frame), `gen/screens` | `gen/App.*`, `gen/screens` |
| `apps/magazine` | svelte | `src/lib` (TypeScript only: state, corpus, design, tokens) | `src/App.svelte`, `src/reference`, `src/parts`, `src/feed`, `src/templates` | `src/App.svelte`, `src/reference`, `src/templates` |
| `apps/discovery` | svelte | none | `src/App.svelte`, `src/parts` | `src/parts/panorama-view.svelte`, `screen-preview.svelte`, `theme-corner.svelte` |
| `packages/taste-screens` | svelte | `src/recipes` | `src/screens`, `src/parts` | `src/screens` |

## Vocabulary

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Raw HTML injection | Rendering an HTML string as markup instead of building nodes. |
| Dynamic tag | Choosing the host element at run time from a value. |
| Raw native tag | A lowercase HTML element name written in a composition template. |
| Reactive ARIA state | An `aria-*` attribute whose value is an expression of state or props. |
| Component root | The first rendered node of a component file, ignoring control flow wrappers. |
| Literal text | Visible or announced words written in the template or in a text prop instead of coming from content. |
| Two-way binding | A binding that writes back into the parent state. |

The per-runtime syntax of each term is in the runtime appendix of that stack.

## The gate

`bun run check` runs the rules gate (`packages/tooling/rules/rules.ts --gate`): per-runtime adapters
parse every composition file into one small tree, and shared detectors report
`block-root`, `raw-html`, `dynamic-tag`, `raw-native-tag`, `reactive-aria` and
`literal-text`. The kit zone is never scanned. Existing violations are recorded
per package in `rules/baselines/<package>.json`; a new one fails the check.

The host frame `gen/App.*` of each host app is composition and block root: it opens on
`Block tag="main"` and is built from kit primitives; the dynamic screen loader lives in the
kit zone (`gen/runtime/ScreenOutlet.*` for React and Vue). In `apps/magazine`, `src/lib`
holds TypeScript only; markup lives in `src/parts`, `src/templates` and `src/reference`.
The style groups (`corners`, `shadows`, `hardcode`, `spacing`) also scan the magazine style text
against `rules/style-baselines/magazine.json`.

## Outside every zone

Three.js and canvas engine code is not UI composition and is out of all rules (00 to 06 and the
style groups): `packages/panorama` declares no `ui8kit` field, is absent from `rules/zones.json`,
has no `rules/baselines` or `rules/style-baselines` file, and is never scanned. A Svelte part
that only mounts such an engine (a canvas host) stays in its app's composition zone.
